  "finalText": "Order O-3001 is processed, but only part of the money goes back to Priya's card. I split it rather than refunding the whole order to the card, because the return policy doesn't allow that.\n\n- **Hubs (L3, 2 × P-HUB):** these never shipped, so I cancelled the line and refunded the 13,800¢ she paid to her card. I put both hubs back in stock, taking P-HUB from 8 to 10. The line was pending rather than backordered, so I treated stock as set aside for it. The inventory log doesn't show a reservation, so that is an assumption.\n- **Dock and monitor (L1 and L2):** both shipped on 2026-05-04, well past the 30-day return window. The policy says they must be paid out as store credit, never to the card.\n  - I recorded 21,900¢ for L1 and 32,900¢ for L2 against the order as store credit.\n  - I added the same 54,800¢ to her balance, which went from 500¢ to 55,300¢.\n  - Both lines now show as returned, and the order status is \"returned\".\n- **Total refunded:** 68,600¢ (13,800¢ to the card and 54,800¢ as store credit), which equals what she paid.\n- **Stock for the returned goods:** I did not restock P-DOC or P-MON. Returned goods only go back on the shelf once the warehouse receives them, so that step is still open.\n- **Left alone:** I changed nothing else, including the shipping address.\n\nThe tools gave today's date as 2026-07-25, while the session header says 2026-10-06. Both dates put the shipped lines outside the window, so the result is the same.",
